{"entryId":"1766","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1766:1","sourceSha256":"8d0584d0942af971bfde1bc017f80504061b13375d7910482b9e2f2602dbc0e3","englishSha256":"d5df59dba4f8eb9a0be4df450f7bc8d4919760d008b79b821e7fd6625b103971","citations":[{"id":"1766:1:citation-01","he":[0,83],"en":[60,73],"target":{"entry":2380,"paragraph":10},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 2380:10","assessment":"Chullin gives Yehoshua ben Zeruz in the report before Rabbi, states the kinship, and names Beit Shean. The received Ziron spelling is preserved.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2380:10","target":{"entry":2380,"paragraph":10},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Chullin 6b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_6b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1766:1:citation-02","he":[0,83],"en":[135,145],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_6b.5"},"reference":"Chullin 6b:5","assessment":"Chullin gives Yehoshua ben Zeruz in the report before Rabbi, states the kinship, and names Beit Shean. The received Ziron spelling is preserved.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 6b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_6b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2380:10","target":{"entry":2380,"paragraph":10},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"1766:1:citation-03","he":[85,127],"en":[150,162],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_147a.9"},"reference":"Shabbat 147a:9","assessment":"Shabbat 147a gives ben Ziruz as the first voice in the cloak incident and ben Kefusai as Ravin’s alternative. This is in Chavit. The distinct Tolin pointer was not located in the checked loci.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 147a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_147a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 147a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat